<title>USA: Empi Inc says acquisition debt paid.</title>
<headline>Empi Inc says acquisition debt paid.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Empi Inc said Tuesday that all the remaining debt related to its 1992 acquisition of Medtronic Inc's Nortech division was paid off in the third quarter.</p>
<p>This leaves the company essentially debt-cash available for corporate purposes, the medical devices maker said.</p>
<p>Earlier Tuesday, the company reported net income of $2.4 million or $0.28 a share in the third quarter, compared to $2.1 million, or $0.24 a share a year ago.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
